{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They shall be baked with leaven, as first fruits.</b> The omer was the first fruits of barley, and these were the first fruits of the wheat harvest. The festival is called יוֹם הַבִּכּוּרִים after them, as it says (Numbers 28:26): וּבְיוֹם הַבִּכּוּרִים בְּהַקְרִיבְכֶם מִנְחָה חֲדָשָׂה. It says לַה׳ because through them the new grain was permitted for offering. And since this is in the nature of thanksgiving for the decrees of harvest during which the produce was at risk, the two breads were leavened, brought as inner offerings together with the lambs of shelamim, just as was the case with the shelamim of thanksgiving (Leviticus 7:13), upon loaves of leavened bread."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:29.885586898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}